What is Java? 

- Java  is object oriented programming  language .
- Java was developed by James Gosling at Sun Microsystems in the year 1995.

Features:

 1) Platform Independent:
      -Write once , Run anywhere, java achive this feature through the JVM. (java virtual machine)
      -the compiler compile the source code into byte-code(.class)
      -the byte-code is interpreted by the JVM and convert into platform specific-code,
       the JVM is available for all platforms.
      -as a result, Java pgm compiled on windows can run on any other platforms.


 2) Object-Oriented:
      -Java is fully object-oriented, almost everything in java is an object.
      -it support all concepts like : (encapsulation,inheritance, abstraction, polymorpism)

 3) Secure & Robust: 
     -Java incorporates features like.
        -> byte-code-verifier.
        -> exception-handling.
        -> garbage collector.(automatically identify & Reclaim unused memory occupied by objects in pgms)
        -> and avoid pointers for security.

 4) Multithreading:
      -process of handling multiple tasks simultaneously.
      -java pgms devided into multiple parts called thread.
      -these are executed paralaly, so we don't need to wait for completion of another tasks.
        


